mark@tfsg.UUCP (Mark Crafts) writes:

>Can someone explain Stridence to me?
>The doc file that came with my version doesn't even acknowledge it's
>existence.  I assume that "Lawful S:850" Means "Lawful with a 
>stridence of 850," but how do you increase/decrease stridence and what
>exactly does it do for you?
No it doesn't mean this. The S means Score, so your current score is
about 850 points, which is (more or less) what you will get when you
die or exit the dungeon. Please not that there is a (10% ?) penalty
for dying and when leaving the dungeon, your jewellery and pets are
added to the bones, an the total is doubled when carrying the Amulet.
You will see the Score increase on the killing of each monster.

